  "lesson3Card1Title": "What is an if statement?",
  "@lesson3Card1Speech": {
    "description": "Lesson 3 text. Very simple English: short sentences, one idea each. if, elif, else, True, False and `backticks` are code: keep them in English."
  },
  "lesson3Card1Speech": "Every day you make choices. If it rains, you bring an umbrella. Programs make choices too! We use `if` for that.",
  "lesson3Card1Tip": "`if` lets the program choose what to do.",
  "lesson3Card2Title": "The shape of an if",
  "lesson3Card2Speech": "An `if` has a shape. First, write `if`. Next, write a question. The answer must be `True` or `False`. Then, write a colon `:`. Last, indent the next line. That line runs only when the answer is `True`.",
  "lesson3Card2Tip": "Indent means spaces in front of the line. Use 4 spaces.",
  "lesson3Card3Title": "Comparing values",
  "lesson3Card3Speech": "Python can compare two values. The answer is always `True` or `False`. Here are six ways to compare.",
  "lesson3Card3Tip": "`!=` means not equal. `>=` means bigger or equal.",
  "lesson3Card4Title": "Warning: = is not ==",
  "lesson3Card4Speech": "Be careful! These two look alike. One `=` puts a value in a box. Two `==` ask a question. They ask: are these equal?",
  "lesson3Card4Tip": "In an `if`, you almost always need `==`.",
  "lesson3Card5Title": "else: when it is False",
  "lesson3Card5Speech": "What if the answer is `False`? Use `else`. The `else` part runs when the question is `False`. Only one part runs, never both.",
  "lesson3Card5Tip": "`else` has no question. It still needs a colon `:`.",
  "lesson3Card6Title": "elif: more choices",
  "lesson3Card6Speech": "Sometimes you have more than two choices. Use `elif` for that. Python checks each question from top to bottom. The first `True` one runs. Then Python stops checking.",
  "lesson3Card6Tip": "`elif` is short for else if.",
  "lesson3Card7Title": "Indent matters",
  "lesson3Card7Speech": "Python uses spaces to see what goes inside the `if`. No spaces means an error. Always indent the lines under the `if`.",
  "lesson3Card7Tip": "Put 4 spaces in front of each line inside the `if`.",
  "lesson3Card8Title": "Recap: the whole shape",
  "lesson3Card8Speech": "Great job! Here is the whole shape on one screen. Look at each part.",
  "lesson3Card8Tip": "`if` first. Then `elif`. Then `else`. Each one ends with `:`. Indent the lines under them.",
  "lesson3NoteAskBattery": "is battery less than 20?",
  "lesson3NoteRunsIfTrue": "runs only if the answer is True",
  "lesson3NoteShapeIf": "if + question + colon (:)",
  "lesson3NoteShapeIndent": "4 spaces in front: runs only when True",
  "lesson3NoteEq": "equal? True",
  "lesson3NoteNotEq": "not equal? True",
  "lesson3NoteGreater": "bigger? True",
  "lesson3NoteLess": "smaller? False",
  "lesson3NoteGreaterEq": "bigger or equal? True",
  "lesson3NoteLessEq": "smaller or equal? False",
  "lesson3NoteAssign": "one =: puts 3 in the box",
  "lesson3NoteCompare": "two ==: asks if lives is 3",
  "lesson3NoteBattery50": "battery is 50",
  "lesson3NoteCheck50": "is 50 less than 20? False",
