  "lesson6Card1Speech": "You win 2 coins in a game. Then you win 3 more. How many coins now? 5! You added them in your head. Python can do math too, just like a calculator. Put the math inside `print()` to see the answer.",
  "lesson6Card1Tip": "Python works out the math first. Then `print` shows the answer.",
  "lesson6Card2Title": "Add and subtract: + and -",
  "lesson6Card2Speech": "Use `+` to add and `-` to subtract. You beat an enemy, so your score goes up. You get hit, so you lose a life. We keep each answer in a variable.",
  "lesson6Card2Tip": "The math on the right runs first. Then the answer goes into the box on the left.",
  "lesson6Card3Title": "Warning: / gives a decimal",
  "lesson6Card3Speech": "Use `*` to multiply and `/` to divide. Careful! `/` always gives a number with a decimal point. So `10 / 2` gives `5.0`, not `5`. Remember Lesson 2? A number with a decimal point is a `float`.",
  "lesson6Card3Tip": "`/` always gives a `float`, even when the answer is a whole number.",
  "lesson6Card4Title": "Teams and left over: // and %",
  "lesson6Card4Speech": "We have 7 robots. We make teams of 2. `//` divides and keeps only the whole number. So `7 // 2` gives 3 full teams. `%` gives what is left over. So `7 % 2` gives 1 robot with no team.",
  "lesson6Card4Tip": "`//` counts the full teams. `%` counts who is left over.",
  "lesson6Card5Title": "Power: **",
  "lesson6Card5Speech": "Two stars `**` mean power. `2 ** 3` means 2 * 2 * 2. Three 2s multiplied. That gives 8. Careful! It is not the same as `2 * 3`. That gives 6.",
  "lesson6Card5Tip": "One star `*` multiplies. Two stars `**` is power.",
  "lesson6Card6Title": "Order: what goes first?",
  "lesson6Card6Speech": "There are 2 red robots and 3 blue robots. Each robot has 4 wheels. How many wheels in all? We want 20. But `2 + 3 * 4` gives 14. Why? Python does `*` and `/` first. Then it does `+` and `-`. Put `( )` around what must go first.",
  "lesson6Card6Tip": "Multiply and divide go first, then add and subtract. `( )` go before everything.",
  "lesson6Card7Title": "Math with variables",
  "lesson6Card7Speech": "You can do math with a variable. `score = score + 10` adds 10 to the score. The short way is `score += 10`. It does the same thing! Remember the `while` loop in Lesson 4? `battery = battery - 1` can be `battery -= 1`.",
  "lesson6Card7Tip": "`+=` adds to the old value. `-=` takes away from it.",
  "lesson6Card8Title": "Recap: math operators",
  "lesson6Card8Speech": "Great job! Here are all the operators on one screen. Each one uses 7 and 2.",
  "lesson6Card8Tip": "Remember: `/` gives a decimal, `( )` go first, and `+=` is the short way to add.",
