  "lesson7Title": "Strings",
  "lesson7Card1Title": "What is a string?",
  "@lesson7Card1Speech": {
    "description": "Lesson 7 text. Very simple English: short sentences, one idea each. string, str, len, upper, lower, character, error and `backticks` are code words: keep them in English."
  },
  "lesson7Card1Speech": "Look at my name tag. It says Cog. That is text! In Python, text inside quotes is called a string. Remember `str` from Lesson 2? `str` is short for string.",
  "lesson7Card1Tip": "A string is text inside quotes, like `\"Cog\"`.",
  "lesson7Card2Title": "Single or double quotes",
  "lesson7Card2Speech": "You can use single quotes `'Hi'` or double quotes `\"Hi\"`. Both work! But the start and the end must match. A string that starts with `\"` must end with `\"`.",
  "lesson7Card2Tip": "Pick one kind of quote. Use it at both ends.",
  "lesson7Card3Title": "Joining strings: +",
  "lesson7Card3Speech": "Use `+` to join strings. `\"Hi, \" + \"Cog\"` gives `Hi, Cog`. Look at the space after the comma. It is inside the quotes. Python only adds the spaces you type!",
  "lesson7Card3Tip": "Need a space? Put it inside the quotes.",
  "lesson7Card4Title": "Repeating strings: *",
  "lesson7Card4Speech": "In Lesson 6, `*` multiplied numbers. With a string, `*` repeats it! `\"Ha\" * 3` gives `HaHaHa`. Great for a robot laugh or a game banner.",
  "lesson7Card4Tip": "A string `*` a number repeats the string that many times.",
  "lesson7Card5Title": "Counting characters: len()",
  "lesson7Card5Speech": "`len()` counts the characters in a string. A character is one letter, number, or space. `len(\"Cog\")` gives 3. `len(\"Hi Cog\")` gives 6, because the space counts too!",
  "lesson7Card5Tip": "Spaces are characters too. `len()` counts them.",
  "lesson7Card6Title": "Warning: counting starts at 0",
  "lesson7Card6Speech": "Use `[ ]` to pick one character. Careful! Python counts from 0, not 1. So `\"Cog\"[0]` is `C`. And `\"Cog\"[2]` is `g`. Remember `range(3)` from Lesson 4? It also starts at 0: 0, 1, 2.",
  "lesson7Card6Tip": "The first character is `[0]`, not `[1]`.",
  "lesson7Card7Title": "Warning: text and numbers do not mix",
  "lesson7Card7Speech": "Big warning! `\"5\"` is text. `5` is a number. You cannot join them with `+`. Python shows an error. To fix it, make both text, or both numbers. `str()` turns a number into text.",
  "lesson7Card7Tip": "Use `str()` to put a number inside a message, like a score.",
  "lesson7Card8Title": "Big and small letters",
  "lesson7Card8Speech": "`.upper()` makes every letter big. `.lower()` makes every letter small. Write it right after the string, with a dot in front. Robots shout in big letters!",
  "lesson7Card8Tip": "`.upper()` for BIG letters. `.lower()` for small letters.",
  "lesson7Card9Title": "Recap: strings",
  "lesson7Card9Speech": "Great job! Here are all your string tools on one screen.",
  "lesson7Card9Tip": "Remember: spaces count, `[0]` is first, and use `str()` before joining a number.",
